<article class="env-example" id="02PE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02PE">Example <span data-tag="02PE">42.68.11</span>.</a> Consider the local ring $R = \mathbf{Z}_ p$. Set $M = \mathbf{Z}_ p/(p^2) \oplus \mathbf{Z}_ p/(p^3)$. Let $u : M \to M$ be the map given by the matrix </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  u = \left( \begin{matrix}  a 

&  b 

\\  pc 

&  d 

\end{matrix} \right)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $a, b, c, d \in \mathbf{Z}_ p$, and $a, d \in \mathbf{Z}_ p^*$. In this case $\det _\kappa (u)$ equals multiplication by $a^2d^3 \bmod p \in \mathbf{F}_ p^*$. This can easily be seen by consider the effect of $u$ on the symbol $[p^2e, pe, pf, e, f]$ where $e = (0 , 1) \in M$ and $f = (1, 0) \in M$. </p>
</article>